# FEX on Aurora

This is FEX built from Aurora's fork (https://github.com/aurora-silicon/fex),
packaged as fex-emu. It provides `fex` and replaces the FEX-Emu package from
the Asahi ALARM repository, so `pacman -S fex`, `pacman -S fex-emu` and
`pacman -S FEX-Emu` all install it.

## 4 KiB pages

FEX needs a 4 KiB page size. Aurora kernels use 16 KiB pages but can give a
process tree 4 KiB pages when the kernel is booted with `user4k=on` (the
default on Aurora images; `aurora-userpages` adds it to the GRUB command line).
Start x86 programs inside a 4 KiB tree:

    userpages 4k FEXBash
    userpages 4k FEXInterpreter ./program

Programs started from a 4 KiB tree inherit it, including x86 programs that
binfmt_misc hands to FEXInterpreter. Started from an ordinary 16 KiB process,
FEX runs with 16 KiB pages and x86 programs fail. `userpages --status` shows
the current page size. Aurora's Steam launcher starts Steam in a 4 KiB tree.

## Hardware TSO

On kernels that offer the memory-model prctl (PR_SET_MEM_MODEL), FEX switches
the process to the hardware total store order mode and drops its software
TSO emulation. Check with:

    FEXGetConfig --tso-emulation-info

## Root filesystem

FEX reads x86 root filesystems from /usr/share/fex-emu/RootFS and
~/.local/share/fex-emu/RootFS; `FEXRootFSFetcher` fetches one. Steam's x86
titles use the Steam runtime instead.

## Thunks

This build has no host library thunks (as the FEX-Emu package it replaces).
